  <p class="lead">
    Real estate, stock investments, and property rentals form a central component of wealth creation in the UK. However, navigating the intricate framework of <strong>Capital Gains Tax (CGT)</strong> and <strong>Rental Income Tax</strong> rules requires meticulous record-keeping, strategic foresight, and strict compliance with <strong>HM Revenue & Customs (HMRC)</strong> guidelines.
  </p>
  <p>
    Whether you are a seasoned portfolio landlord, a first-time buy-to-let investor, or an individual selling inherited property or high-value shares, understanding the tax implications of your decisions is paramount. Over the past few years, the UK government has implemented sweeping changes to property taxation, including a dramatic reduction in the Capital Gains Tax allowance, shifts in residential property CGT rates, and the ongoing impact of Section 24 on mortgage interest relief.
  </p>
  <p>
    This comprehensive, expertly curated guide breaks down the essential rules, allowances, and reporting requirements for the 2025/2026 tax year, ensuring you remain compliant while optimizing your tax position according to current E-E-A-T (Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, and Trustworthiness) principles.
  </p>

